"""Append a new recount section only after verifying the entire old ledger prefix."""
from pathlib import Path
import hashlib,json
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;R=P.parents[1]
ledger=R/'design/PREMISE-LEDGER-20261025.md';data=ledger.read_bytes()
prefix=json.loads((P/'Rc6_ledger_prefix.json').read_text());n=prefix['bytes']
assert len(data)>=n and hashlib.sha256(data[:n]).hexdigest()==prefix['sha256'],'Existing sections changed'
x=json.loads((P/'Rc6_premises.json').read_text())
marker='## Recount on Rc6_Top (2026-10-26)'
assert marker.encode() not in data,'Already appended'
lines=['',marker,'','**S2 OPEN; target not yet established.** Actual theorem: `AspisR1.Rc6_Top.deployed`. Base: `AspisR1.Rc5_Top.deployed`. This is a new section; all preceding bytes were checked unchanged against `evidence/recount6-20261026/Rc6_ledger_prefix.json`.','','Method: fresh kernel `#check @...` / `#print` inventories of the root, nested result/caller/continuation/finish, trust structures, game and runtime dictionary; quantified atomic families, shared witnesses/guards and non-alias dictionary deduplication follow the original ledger. Classification and row-to-field correspondence are reviewed; counts are mechanical. The machine-readable rows, diff and source/log hashes are in `evidence/recount6-20261026/Rc6_premises.json`; expanded structure fields are in `Rc6_field_catalog.json`.','','| Scope | Before T/P/C | After T/P/C | Lead T/P/C | Session A T/P/C | External T/P/C |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
fmt=lambda d:'/'.join(str(d[c]) for c in ['T','P','C'])
for scope,v in x['counts'].items():
 lines.append('| '+scope+' | '+fmt(x['before_counts'][scope]['classes'])+' | '+fmt(v['classes'])+' | '+' | '.join(fmt(v['by_owner'][o]) for o in ['lead','session A','external'])+' |')
lines+=['','The actual antecedent delta is **0T, −1P, 0C** (L099); the additional deployment delta is **0T, −5P, 0C** (L195–L199). Deduplicated total: **89T+46P → 89T+40P**, with eleven approved game-domain clauses retained. Excluding those clauses explicitly gives **89T+35P → 89T+29P**. No new premise or trust item is added. The seven SessionAPrepare leaves N108–N114 and parser rows L129–L132 were already absent on Rc5 and receive no duplicate removal credit.','','Before: the nested Rc5 caller requires `P2Prime → FirstEntryVerifierConeJoin → ∃ parsed, facts ∧ sites ∧ Rc5_Cont.Outcome`. After: Rc6 requires `P2Prime → ∃ parsed, facts ∧ sites ∧ Rc5_Cont.Outcome`; the same result witnesses additionally carry `PFin_Packet.Facts`, `P6C_OnCuts.SafeBatches` and `P6C_FullBoundary.Facts`. The explicit root binders, frozen3 carrier/game/failure events, query budgets and numerical bounds are unchanged. Full before/after statements are retained in `Rc6_before-statement.lean.txt` and `Rc6_after-statement.lean.txt`.','','`Rc6_Result.strengthen` uses the existing Rc5 f/s/run/tx2 and checkpoint version for every addition. `Rc6_Install.parser_base`, `p6_base`, `reconstruct` prove dictionary compatibility; `Rc6_Statements.reverse` transports the entire conclusion back to Rc5 on the same inputs. `Rc6_Equivalent.same_domain` proves relative result-domain equivalence under the retained extraction/oracle premises. `Rc6_Nonvacuity.accepted_input` preserves the conditional accepted input and excludes an always-rejecting driver; it does not instantiate all top premises jointly. JFx_ retains that joint fixture obligation.','','P6 removal is accepted-run refinement on the original issued ordered logs plus the defined ideal extension; it is not a universal totality claim about an unissued native syscall. `P6C_CarrierGap.independent` explains why mathematical P6 closure does not remove L166. Frozen3/global source and runtime carrier association remain.','','### Row diff against Rc5','','| ID | Class | Owner | Scope | Change | Evidence |','|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
for r in x['diff']:
 lines.append('| '+' | '.join(str(r.get(k,'')).replace('|','/') for k in ['id','classification','owner','scope','change'])+' | '+(r.get('theorem','unchanged atomic family; fresh Rc6 inventories'))+' |')
lines+=['','### Remaining P coverage','','Tags identify covering jobs only; none imports closure from a concurrent branch. JFx_ covers fixture instantiation, not universal discharge of accepted-event/P2Prime/game clauses. `UNCOVERED` means no listed job is credited for that row.','','| ID | Owner | Scope | Covering job | Remaining family |','|---|---|---|---|---|']
for r in x['rows']:
 if r['classification']=='P':lines.append('| '+' | '.join(str(r[k]).replace('|','/') for k in ['id','owner','scope','running_job','name'])+' |')
lines+=['','**Release gates:** L187 remains `UNCOVERED`: coherent frozen dependency replay. L188 remains `UNCOVERED`: final release-wide trust/axiom audit. The focused Rc6 standard-axiom check discharges neither release gate. L186 source lowering to the frozen default/devnet/Pool artifacts also remains.','','Validation: 100/100 Lean compile attempts (8 proof modules and 92 focused inventories), 0/10 Kani, no package replay. Per-attempt exact target, command, exit, wall time, peak RSS, swap, source revision/hash, dependency fingerprints and axioms are retained under `evidence/recount6-20261026/`. All new top theorems have `#print axioms` using only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`. One 6G/8G/Swap0/Tasks64 scope at a time, Lean `-M7000`; no cap increases or timeout/memory-kill reruns. The cache inventory pins 1,726 selected modules; two inherited comment-only source variants are recorded separately. This is focused cache composition, not a fresh frozen-release replay. No shipped file or cfg(kani) harness changed, so the ELF rebuild trigger did not fire.','']
section='\n'.join(lines).encode();ledger.write_bytes(data+section)
(P/'Rc6_ledger_append_check.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(previous_bytes=n,previous_sha256=prefix['sha256'],prefix_intact=True,appended_bytes=len(section),appended_sha256=hashlib.sha256(section).hexdigest(),new_bytes=ledger.stat().st_size,new_sha256=hashlib.sha256(ledger.read_bytes()).hexdigest()),indent=2)+'\n')
print('Verified old ledger prefix and appended',len(section),'bytes')
